{
	title: 'Browser client with the terminal features',
	description: 'One page doing what the terminal client does, served by the p6 endpoint. Without the cookie it shows a password field; after one successful login it goes straight to the conversation on later visits. It connects to /ws, opens the newest session (or creates one), and folds events with the same common transcript.fold the terminal uses, so both show the same transcript: prompts, thinking (dimmed), streamed text, tool calls and results, turn ends ([cancelled], [interrupted], errors) and rejected notices. A textarea submits on Enter (Shift+Enter is a newline); Escape cancels a running turn. On disconnect it reconnects with backoff and takes the fresh snapshot, like a restarted terminal. Keep it tiny: plain DOM, no framework or CSS library, no build step beyond Bun bundling the TS at request time (or at startup). Code lives in src/web/ (browser only; imports web and common, never host or client); extend the conventions test and tasks/README.md for this layer. Test the page logic that is not DOM (view from events, reconnect) with plain unit tests, and one end-to-end check that the served bundle loads and logs in, using a headless browser only if one is already installed.',
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['p6']
}
